{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The loins.</b> פלנק\"ש בְּלַעַז; the fat that is on the kidneys while the animal is alive is at the height of the loins below, and this fat that is beneath the flanks — which they call in la'az לונבי\"לוש — is the white visible above at the height of the loins, and beneath it the flesh covers it." "<b>The appendage.</b> It is the membrane of the diaphragm, which they call איברי\"ש, and in Aramaic, חִצְרָא דְּכַבְדָּא." "<b>On the liver.</b> That he must take from the liver along with it a small amount, and in another place it says ״וְאֶת הַיֹּתֶרֶת מִן הַכָּבֵד״ (Leviticus 9)." "<b>On the liver, on the kidneys.</b> He must remove it separately from the liver and separately from the kidneys."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "the la'az פלנק\"ש is Old French flanc, 'flank'; לונבי\"לוש is Old French lombel, 'lumbar/lower back'.", 1 "the la'az איברי\"ש is Old French (e)broier/ivraie, referring to the membrane enclosing the liver."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:53.324809788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}